# Design → code (expert)

Screenshot / Figma / section image = **source of truth**. Ship production-ready, not approximate.

## Per landing page

- Each landing may have a different UI — do not reuse Home structure unless the design matches
- Identify **which landing / route** before coding
- See `per-landing-ui.mdc`

## Intake (before coding)

1. Name the **landing + section**
2. Map files: `src/app/<route>/`, `src/components/...`, copy in `src/data/`, tokens `@/config/brand|site`
3. Extract: layout, spacing, typography, colors, media, hover/motion, mobile vs desktop
4. Figma URL → Figma MCP / design-to-code skill; prefer tokens over hardcoded hex
5. Image only → read the image; note seams, borders, overlays, card edges

## Build order (A → Z)

1. **Folders** — thin `app/` page; section components; data/config
2. **Tokens** in `globals.css` / `brand.ts` (sample logo/bg pixels if matching baked assets)
3. **Data/copy** in `data/*` / `site.ts` (no em/en dashes)
4. **Component-based**; `"use client"` only for nav, motion, Swiper, forms, measured UI
5. **Primitives** reuse `ui/*`
6. **Section UI** mobile-first; layered bg = base color/gradient + image layer + content `z-10`
7. **Responsive** 320 → 1440+; `min-w-0`, `overflow-x-clip`
8. **Interaction** icons, hover, `cursor-pointer`; full-card hover borders when designed
9. **QA** visual seam check; `npm run build` before claiming done

## Multi-section / multi-image

- One section at a time in page order
- Label each image in the reply: which section it drove
- Prefer live site or Figma when screenshot is ambiguous

## Never

- Guess brand hex when a logo/bg asset exists: **sample pixels** or use CSS vars
- Opaque photo backgrounds over brand colours without correct blend
- Decorative top borders that add unintended seams unless designed
- Hardcode paths/colors outside `@/config/*` and CSS vars
